    "result_text": "Done. The test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `sharesHousehold` opt-out already existed; the new work was to assign and return a shared `householdId`. I kept structural impact low by putting the real logic in the tiny `Households` helper class (low surrounding complexity) and touching each large class with a single small addition.\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `householdId` string to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it and MapStruct auto-maps it (same pattern as `customerCode`). No mapper change needed.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `household_id` column field plus a plain getter/setter (CC 1 each).\n\n3. **`Households.java`** (the small cohesive unit) \u2014 added `joinHousehold(...)`: when `sharesHousehold` is true and matching housemates exist, it stamps the candidate and every existing housemate with a **stable, deterministic** id (`UUID.nameUUIDFromBytes` over the normalized `lastName|address` key) and returns the housemates to persist. Reusing the existing `sameHousehold`/`normalize` helpers keeps it tiny. The id is stable, so joiners at the same address always converge on the same value regardless of order.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 one added statement that calls `joinHousehold(...)` and saves the affected housemates, right before the candidate itself is saved.\n\n5. **DB (hsqldb, the profile the tests use)** \u2014 added the `household_id` column to `schema.sql` (ddl-auto is `none` there) and padded the ten positional owner rows in `data.sql`. The default `h2` app profile uses `ddl-auto=update`, so it self-heals without a schema edit.\n\nBoth housemates and later joiners receive the identical, non-blank `householdId`, satisfying the spec and the acceptance test's `assertEquals(hb, ...householdId)` / `assertTrue(!hb.isBlank())`.",
